tion for write verbs), or explicitly capture the pre-mutation state if a true at-operation-time reading is required.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.215,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Detector reads live state itself: `state = show_ticket(ticket_id, repo_root=repo_root)` (src/rebar/_commands/cross_session.py:39)","Write handlers call `_ack()` after the mutation, e.g. `rebar.tag(ticket_id, tag); return _ack()` (src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:423-424)","For in-scope verbs the mutation does not change the holder, so the cross-session signal still surfaces — the ordering claim is a mis-description, not a functional break"],"finding":"The plan states the warning 'reflects the ticket state at operation time (read before a mutation applies)', but in the write handlers `_ack()` is invoked AFTER `rebar.<mutation>(...)` and `cross_session_warning_for` performs its own fresh `show_ticket` read at that point — so the detector actually reads state AFTER the mutation, not before it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff71aed09d46fb877","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'The warning reflects the ticket state at operation time (read before a mutation applies).'","norm_id":"n98779f990c71d6da","priority":0.385,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future in-scope verb (or edit_ticket) that could alter holder/status would read the POST-mutation state, contradicting the 'read before' contract as written"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","