 not omits_required_site)"],"finding":"The leaf narrows the parent epic's MCP-surface coverage: parent AC3 expects the cross-session warning surfaced on 'single-ticket-targeted operations' over MCP (the parent's design names 'transition' among single-ticket mutations), but the leaf defers the single-ticket MCP mutation tools transition_ticket and reopen_ticket (plus check_ac and declare_no_file_impact) to a follow-up ticket because their response contracts cannot carry a WriteAckOut/TicketStateOut field. This is consistent narrowing (the parent's system-wide goal is preserved via the CLI sibling story and a discovered_from follow-up is tracked), not a contract contradiction — but the deferral of parent-named single-ticket mutation verbs on the very surface this child owns is worth making explicit against parent AC3.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f685b2528b507c9bd","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Accepted scope limits (documented, not covered by this story)'","norm_id":"n74ff3c856e699d81","priority":0.22,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An MCP client runs transition_ticket / reopen_ticket on an A-held ticket as session B and receives no structured cross-session_warning field, even though the parent epic's AC3 lists MCP single-ticket-mutation coverage as in-scope for the per-surface stories."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"a